    "millsfield:images_texts": [
      "FACTORY OFFICE\nFOOT OF JUNIPER STREET\nRYAN AIRLINES, INC.\nBUILDERS OF AIRCRAFT\nOPERATORS\nLOS ANGELES - SAN DIEGO AIRLINE\nSAN DIEGO, CALIF.,\nMar. 26,1927\nDear Mr. Biphy:\nI remind your tikoram, thee day late,\nthou my return from Las Angeles, and flew one of\nthe Ryan Cabin planco to a field tua miles from her. Munto\nshop the nept day.\nI he motor, as l wined you, is a combination\nof g. 4. and g. 1. Whiskwindo with g. 1. cranbeare and\ncylindes, It has had very little time since overhaul,\nprobably less than ten haurs; but the mayrity of part\nhave sen several hundred hours service. I he crankcase\nhas been welded in at land one ploce and both\nappearance and inguing indicate that the engine\nis largely assembled from Army and hany salvage.\nIt is now installed in a plane built from\na combiation of was material and is easy starting\nand in serviceable condition, but under no circumstances\nworth $2,000 which is the cash price asked.",
      "FACTORY OFFICE\nFOOT OF JUNIPER STREET\nRYAN AIRLINES, INC.\nBUILDERS OF AIRCRAFT\nOPERATORS\nLOS ANGELES - SAN DIEGO AIRLINE\nSAN DIEGO, CALIF.,\nIl understand, indirectly, that at one time bath\nship and motor could have been purchased for 500%\nThe propeller is not designed for the tracchair\ntyle of plane and would hardly prove satisfartary. The\ntra g. 1. hides are fairly well wam.\nI he thickirid type motor has given wonderful\nservice here, an the wet coart and the fact that\nthis motor is still giring good service is in\nits lf. a recommendation for the tright corporaton.\nOur monoplane is progressing rapidly and\nthe wing and goochis tanks are nearly completed.\nI spect to be on Rosseult Shild and ready to\ntake off on aps. 28t. providing conditions are mitable\nat that tine. Of course we are still giring july + st\nto the papers here as our stashing date.\nWith best wishs, l remain,\nYours very truly\ncharles 4. Kindlingh."
